<figure class="endpoint-lifecycle" aria-labelledby="endpoint-lifecycle-title">
  <figcaption id="endpoint-lifecycle-title"><span class="content-kicker">Endpoint state over time</span><strong>Pod termination is observed asynchronously—not as one atomic switch.</strong></figcaption>
  <ol class="state-track">
    <li><span>01</span><b>Ready</b><small>ready=true<br/>serving=true</small></li>
    <i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
    <li class="transition"><span>02</span><b>Termination begins</b><small>deletion timestamp<br/>readiness changes</small></li>
    <i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
    <li class="draining"><span>03</span><b>Draining</b><small>terminating=true<br/>ready=false<br/>serving may remain true</small></li>
    <i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
    <li class="removed"><span>04</span><b>Removed</b><small>No longer published<br/>connections finish or close</small></li>
  </ol>
  <div class="observer-track">
    <span>EndpointSlice controller</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i><span>Node proxies</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i><span>Load balancers</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i><span>Clients + connections</span>
  </div>
  <p>Each observer reconciles at a different time. Graceful shutdown aligns readiness, propagation, draining, termination grace, and application behavior.</p>
</figure>

